@0    = ~Who cometh to bother th' Mother-o'-wisps? Who art thou, mortal? Speak!~
@1    = ~Will? Can you say anything?~
@2    = ~We're just adventurers. We were summoned to this place, aaand.... we're not all too happy because of it.~
@3    = ~What are you?~
@4    = ~You're just another monster. Your days end here!~
@5    = ~I am Will, and this is <CHARNAME>. We are happy to see thee, Mother of Wisps. We seek not unnecessary battles.~
@6    = ~And dost it excuse th' distubance thou cause? Hmm, but fine, thou mayest hold thine weapons as Mother shall kill thou not.~
@7    = ~Aye, methinks it hath been centuries since Mother saw as peculiar ones as thou art!~
@8    = ~I am th' Mother-o'-wisps. All th' lights thou hath seen were but ungrateful children of mine. They hath forgotten about their mother! Thou hast slain them? I care not.~
@9    = ~Therr'grath should'st be dead, anyway. Ah, if only mother couldst leave that damn place!~
@10   = ~This one here - it's Will. He is a shaman and I think he can make that wish come true.~
@11   = ~Another monster. Your days end here!~
@12   = ~I'm not sure what to tell you. I think I'll just leave you be.~
@13   = ~Yes. If thou wish it, Mother, I canst bound thee to myself. I mayst show thee places different from this cavern. I may show thee other grottos or even th' world above - lands that do not belong to the Underdark.~
@14   = ~Would'st thou like to see them?~
@15   = ~Ah, tempting, young man... tell thine Mother the price.~
@16   = ~Help us in our mission. That is th' only condition. We wish to stop a mage whom hurt this one here. What sayeth thou?~
@17   = ~Aye, thou hath my support, spectre. Anything wouldst be better than these walls and shrooms!~
@18   = ~Do as thou wish!~
@19   = ~Foolish thing! Thou shalt see Mother's wrath!~
